Fix horizontal scroll wheel on X11 servers.

mapButtonFromX() claimed X11 buttons 6 and 7 (horizontal wheel tilt) as
plain mouse buttons, so onMouseRelease() sent meaningless button-6/7
clicks to clients and its horizontal-wheel branch was unreachable.
Vertical scrolling (buttons 4/5) already fell through to kButtonNone
and worked. Let 6/7 fall through too so they are forwarded as
horizontal wheel events.

diff --git a/src/lib/platform/XWindowsScreen.cpp b/src/lib/platform/XWindowsScreen.cpp
index d8c7bb9..ad6583b 100644
--- a/src/lib/platform/XWindowsScreen.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/platform/XWindowsScreen.cpp
@@ -1740,8 +1740,6 @@ ButtonID XWindowsScreen::mapButtonFromX(const XButtonEvent *event) const
   case 1:
   case 2:
   case 3:
-  case 6:
-  case 7:
     return static_cast<ButtonID>(button); // Handle Left, Middle and Right buttons
   case 8:
     return kButtonExtra0; // Mouse 4
